			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Brainpoop Digital Garden — Plan\n\n**For:** Dommy's philosophy + politics writing\n**Built from:** Google Drive vault (Obsidian / PARA), plus the thesis work already done here\n**Status:** Plan only — nothing published, nothing moved, nothing deleted yet\n\n## The one-sentence version\n\nA Brainpoop digital garden is not another blog feed. It's a public, evergreen map of your thinking: notes that grow over time, link to each other, and let a reader follow an idea from a raw Droping all the way up to your thesis — instead of scrolling past it chronologically and losing it.\n\nBlog = what's new. Garden = what's true so far, and how it connects.\n\n## What you already have (found in Drive)\n\nThis is not starting from zero. It's mostly untangling what exists.\n\n**The trunk — your thesis:**\n- Democracy is not inherently ethical; it is ethical only when citizens are duty-bound to act as informed custodians and decision-makers on society's behalf.\n- The bridge note already in Drive says it cleanly: politics is not the substance, it's where philosophy — metaethics, ontology, epistemology — converge and become power.\n- Supporting work already done here: first-principles definitions + solved/unsolved questions, the FigJam argument map, the \"soft Matrix\" draft (control through the information layer), the four-piece short series outline, and the epistemic-democracy reference note (Estlund, Landemore, Condorcet, Dewey, Ingham).\n\n**The brand — Brainpoop.Blog (01-Projects/Brainpoop.Blog):**\n- **Brainpoop Dropings (BPD1–BPD5+):** short, raw, voice-driven pieces. Examples already in Drive: \"How to End the Voter ID War\" (BPD2), \"The Map Isn't the Territory (And You're Running Out of Gas)\" / \"Grin and Bear It\" (BPD1, the car/gasoline/bear piece), and the \"Stop Debunking, Start Displacing\" script (BPD4).\n- **Segments, ranked in your own notes:**\n  1. **The Narrative Scalpel** — lead segment, weekly Wednesday. \"One precise, darkly humorous surgical takedown of a current contradiction or misinformation campaign,\" with investigative maps, legal translation, philosophical context, zero-tribal satire. Your notes call this the strongest recommendation: precision + dark humor, no other major newsletter owns that metaphor cleanly.\n  2. **Civic Darkroom** — the artistic/archival alternative: developing better judgment, like developing a photo.\n  3. **The Contradiction Lab** — the repeatable, scientific-series feel.\n  4. Also named: Power Poison, Illusion Index (monthly scorecard vibe).\n- **Branding / Positions:** a Positions note (absolute free speech — \"hate speech is free speech, we don't have speech crimes in America,\" same standards for all actors, anti-authoritarian skepticism, no justification of political violence) and a Soul/character profile. See \"Do not publish\" below.\n- **OP ED Article Drafts** folder, plus a Brainpoop.Blog canvas.\n\n**The soil — the rest of the PARA vault:**\n- `02-Areas/Philosophy` — Moral Reasoning, Deontology, Consequentialism, Theory of Power, Epistemology / Street Epistemology, Emotivism\n- `02-Areas/Politics` / American Politics, \"Politics Should Be Boring,\" \"Politics as Applied Epistemology\"\n- `03-Resources/Concepts` — Power frameworks (Foucauldian Power/Knowledge and others), Political Will, American Power/Hegemony\n- `04-Archive/ChatLogs` — raw source material, not garden content\n- **A Digital Gardener prompt already in Drive** (\"Grok Digital Gardener Agent\" / \"Digital Gardener\"): rigorous, interdisciplinary analyst on theories of power; ground claims in Foucault, Gramsci, Bourdieu, Lukes; map across political, economic, cultural, technological, epistemic, biopolitical domains; deconstruct propaganda and manufactured consent; produce clean markdown with wikilinks, YAML frontmatter, and logical hierarchies; flag uncertainty and counterarguments; no partisan cheerleading, no collapsing power = evil / resistance = good. That prompt is, effectively, the garden's editorial rules already written. Adopt it, don't rewrite it.\n\n**The existing public-facing precedent:**\n- The Cornell 7 wiki and the talking-points wiki were both built here as static HTML snapshot sites (search, backlinks, note graph, light/dark, mobile) from markdown vaults, rebuilt on your say-so — not live-synced. That pattern fits a garden perfectly, and it means you already know how the finished thing feels.\n\n## The problems to fix before planting anything\n\n1. **Duplicates everywhere.** Multiple `Brainpoop`, `BrainPoop Political`, and `Philosophy` folders; multiple `Soul.md`, `Positions.md`, `Philosophy.md`, and `BrainPoop.md` copies. No one — including future you — can tell which is canonical.\n2. **Stubs and empty notes.** The Contradiction Lab note is essentially empty; Civic Darkroom is a paragraph; Segments is just a dataview query. A garden with dead links reads as abandoned.\n3. **`.ajson` files are not content.** The large `01-Projects_Brainpoop_Blog_..._md.ajson` files are Smart Connections embedding/index files. They prove the vault was indexed, but they contain no readable note text. Do not migrate them; migrate the `.md` files they point to.\n4. **Dataview / folder-overview / canvas dependencies.** Several notes only work inside Obsidian (dataview tables, folder-overview blocks, `.canvas` files). A public garden needs plain markdown + wikilinks that survive outside Obsidian.\n5. **Private material mixed into the same vault.** See below — this is the one hard rule.\n\n## Do not publish\n\n- **The Soul/character profile** compiled from family group-chat messages (July 2024 – Sept 2025). It names family members and private dynamics. It is useful background for voice, and it stays private forever. Same for `04-Archive/ChatLogs` and anything under `XX-Private`.\n- **Raw chat logs, transcripts, and un-cleaned fragments** that name private people. Garden notes can be *informed* by them; they must not *be* them.\n- Rule of thumb: if a note would embarrass or expose someone who didn't agree to be published, it belongs in the private vault, linked to — never copied into — the garden.\n\n## Garden architecture\n\nKeep the PARA vault private and canonical. The garden is a curated, public *cut* of it — not a mirror of the whole vault.\n\n```\nHome (Start Here)\n├── The Thesis — Democracy, Duty, and Informed Custodians\n│   ├── Definitions (first principles, solved vs. open questions)\n│   ├── The Soft Matrix (control through the information layer)\n│   ├── Epistemic Democracy (Estlund / Landemore / Condorcet)\n│   └── Sortition, and the three lanes (from the duty-bound brief)\n├── Philosophy Beds\n│   ├── Metaethics, Ontology, Epistemology (the foundation trio)\n│   ├── Moral Reasoning — Deontology, Consequentialism, Emotivism\n│   └── Theory of Power — Foucault, Gramsci, Bourdieu, Lukes\n├── Politics Beds\n│   ├── Politics as Applied Epistemology\n│   ├── American Politics / Politics Should Be Boring\n│   ├── Democracy & Voting Rights, Economy, Healthcare\n│   └── Current-events case files (Cornell 7, etc. — linked, not duplicated)\n├── Segments (the show, in garden form)\n│   ├── The Narrative Scalpel (weekly Wednesday, lead)\n│   ├── Civic Darkroom\n│   └── The Contradiction Lab\n├── Brainpoop Dropings (BPD1, BPD2, … — short pieces, kept raw)\n└── Open Questions (the garden's to-do list, in public)\n```\n\n**Growth stages — on every garden note, in the frontmatter:**\n- 🌱 Seedling — a raw idea, a Droping, a question. Unfinished on purpose.\n- 🌿 Sapling — argued once, linked to at least two other notes, needs pushback.\n- 🌳 Evergreen — settled within your framework so far, sourced, linked both ways, safe to cite from a stream or essay.\n\nThis is the key difference from a blog: a Seedling is *supposed* to be unfinished. Publishing unfinished work is the point of a garden, as long as it's labeled.\n\n**Note template (copy this into every new garden note):**\n\n```markdown\n---\ntitle:\nstatus: seedling | sapling | evergreen\ntags: [philosophy | politics | power | thesis]\nthesis-link: # how this connects to the duty-bound thesis, or \"none yet\"\nsources:\nlast-tended: 2026-10-26\n---\n\n## The idea, in one paragraph\n\n## The argument\n\n## The sharpest objection\n\n## Open questions\n\n## Links\n- [[...]]\n```\n\nThe \"sharpest objection\" section is non-negotiable — it's what separates this from a Substack rant feed, and it matches how you've filed pushback questions with every draft so far.\n\n## Build choice (needs your call)\n\n**Option A — recommended for v1: static snapshot site, same as the talking-points wiki.**\nSource stays in markdown (your Obsidian vault, cleaned). I build an HTML snapshot with search, backlinks, and a note graph, and rebuild it only when you say so. Fast, no hosting to babysit, no live-sync breakage, and you already like how the last two turned out.\n\n**Option B — Quartz / Astro garden on GitHub Pages.**\nTrue digital-garden tooling: live graph, backlinks, growth-stage styling, deploy on every push. More setup, more moving parts, and it punishes the duplicate/stub problem harder — so it's a v2 move, after Phase 1 cleanup, not a starting point.\n\n**Option C — Obsidian Publish.**\nSimplest live option, paid, and it publishes whatever the vault contains — which is exactly why the private/public separation above has to be finished first.\n\nMy recommendation: A now, B later if the garden earns it. Do not pick C until the private material is fenced off.\n\n## Phased plan\n\n**Phase 0 — Freeze and fence (one sitting, no writing).**\n- Pick one canonical folder for Brainpoop.Blog and one for Philosophy/Politics; rename the rest `ARCHIVE-duplicate-YYYY-MM-DD`, don't delete yet.\n- Create a `garden/` cut (or a `publish: true` frontmatter flag) that is the *only* thing the public site ever reads from.\n- Move Soul/profile, ChatLogs, and XX-Private out of the publish cut, permanently.\n- List every stub (Contradiction Lab, Civic Darkroom, Segments) as Seedling or cut it from v1.\n\n**Phase 1 — Seed the garden (the v1 launch set, ~12 notes).**\n- Home / Start Here\n- Thesis + Definitions + Open Questions\n- Soft Matrix\n- Epistemic Democracy reference\n- Politics as Applied Epistemology\n- Theory of Power (Foucault / Gramsci / Bourdieu / Lukes, one page, comparative table)\n- Narrative Scalpel — concept page + one finished Scalpel piece\n- Civic Darkroom + Contradiction Lab — concept pages, honestly labeled Seedling if unfinished\n- BPD1 (Map Isn't the Territory), BPD2 (Voter ID War), BPD4 (Stop Debunking, Start Displacing)\n- That's a garden a stranger can walk through end-to-end in 30 minutes and understand what you think.\n\n**Phase 2 — Wire it into your existing work.**\n- Link, don't copy: talking-points wiki topics (Democracy & Voting Rights, Economy, Healthcare, etc.) and Cornell 7 case notes become linked neighbors of garden notes, not duplicates.\n- The Ideas section (Mass Pardon, ICC Warrants, Pepperoni and the Poop, Every Referee Must Be Corrupt, Prompted, Omar Trap) feeds the garden as Seedlings — each gets a thesis-link line saying whether it supports, pressures, or contradicts the duty-bound thesis.\n- Every new Scalpel (Wednesdays) ends as a garden note: the episode is the stream, the note is what stays.\n\n**Phase 3 — Publish and tend.**\n- Publish the snapshot site (Option A).\n- Weekly ritual: one Scalpel → one garden note or one existing note tended (status bumped, objection added, link added).\n- Monthly ritual: prune — one stub finished or cut, one duplicate resolved, one Evergreen re-checked against new developments.\n- Quarterly: re-read the Open Questions page and promote one Seedling to Sapling.\n\n**What success looks like in 3 months:**\nA stranger lands on Home, reads the thesis in 5 minutes, follows one link chain (Thesis → Soft Matrix → Epistemic Democracy → Sortition), and can tell you back what you believe *and* what would change your mind. That's the garden doing what a feed can't.\n\n## Decisions I need from you\n\n1. **Build: A (snapshot, recommended), B (Quartz), or C (Obsidian Publish)?**\n2. **Name/home:** keep it under Brainpoop.Blog, or give the garden its own name? (Your Drive already has a Brainpoop substack note — say if that's the intended home.)\n3. **Language:** keep the Dropings raw and profane as written, or clean them the way the Ideas section was cleaned? The garden can hold both registers, but pick the default for v1.\n4. **Scope of v1:** the 12-note seed set above, or smaller (thesis + Scalpel + 3 Dropings only)?\n\nSay the word on those four and I'll do Phase 0 + Phase 1 — canonical cleanup list first, then the seed garden, then the site.\n",
